# Google OAuth client for Drive sync. Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in.
#
# How to get these (5 minutes, one time):
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/  →  create or pick a project
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Drive API"
#   3. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → External → add yourself under
#      "Test users" (the app stays in Testing mode; no Google review needed,
#      because Granite only asks for the drive.file scope)
#   4. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#      → Application type: "Desktop app"
#   5. Paste the client ID and secret below
#
# The "secret" for a Desktop app client is not confidential — Google's own docs
# say so, since it ships inside every copy of the binary. PKCE is what actually
# protects the exchange, and Granite always sends one.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
